    "details": "<p class=\"isSelectedEnd\"><strong>Telemetrix is a two-round software hackathon built around vehicle telemetry data. The problem statement will be released at the start of the event and will centre on real telemetry like speed, GPS, engine metrics, sensor streams etc. You'll design, build, and demo a working solution.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Bonus Track:</strong></p>\n<p>Our event has partnered up with the AWS student chapter on campus to help expose participants to AWS and its features. You will be given AWS Educate access, which gives you access to AI-Powered starter kits, Amazon bedrock for, EC2 etc. Using AWS wisely in your prototypes can earn you brownie points and exclusive AWS Merch. This will run seperate from the main event.</p>\n<p class=\"isSelectedEnd\"><strong>Round 1 &mdash; System Design:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>You and your team design and implement your solution from scratch within the given timeframe.</li>\n<li>How you structure your approach or build your product is upto you.</li>\n<li>During this round, organizers will go around and discuss ideas, progress, and direction with each team.</li>\n<li>Deliverable: a working prototype.</li>\n</ul>\n<p class=\"isSelectedEnd\"><strong>Round 2 &mdash; Build:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Each team presents their prototype to the judging panel. Judges will dig into your idea, validate edge cases, and ask questions.&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Deliverable: a repository link for your prototype submitted before evaluation begins, and a video demo.</li>\n</ul>",
